(in-ns 'go.arbace.hs) ^{:go/comments [[15 1 "// Frame is a frame of a thread's stack (HES8 (a))."] [19 15 "// a case's slots; an apply frame's arguments"] [22 11 "// the thread's arena's top when the frame was pushed (arena.go)"] [30 8 "// restores the masking state n on return"] [37 1 "// Thread is a Haskell thread: its stack, its resumption, its masking state (0 unmasked, 1 masked"] [38 1 "// uninterruptibly, 2 masked interruptibly: getMaskingState#'s numbers)."] [49 14 "// what it waits on: *MVar, *Thunk, *sleep, stmWait, nil when runnable"] [57 2 "// an interruptible block (MVar, delay, STM retry): an asynchronous exception may be delivered"] [61 1 "// Machine is hsi's machine: the loader, the address space, the threads."] [90 20 "// a pure primop's arguments"] [91 20 "// a tail call's arguments"] [102 1 "// hsFatal is an error of hsi itself (a class at the check: unimplemented, an impossible state)."] [105 1 "// exitNow ends the program (shutdownHaskellAndExit, an uncaught exception in the main thread)."] [112 1 "// NewMachine is a machine over the STG of the units in libs and the program in prog."] [151 1 "// blockedE is returned by a node whose thread blocked: its resumption is set already."] [154 1 "// enterValue evaluates a value: a thunk entered, anything else returned."] [163 1 "// enter evaluates a thunk: its value, or its code under an update frame, the thunk blackholed."] [181 3 "// another thread evaluates it: wait for its update"] [196 4 "// evaluated in place (newThunkN)"] [205 1 "// update overwrites a thunk with its value."] [209 30 "// the fields and the frame may live in the thunk's own allocation"] [220 1 "// apply calls f with args (eval/apply: exact, partial, over-saturated)."] [260 1 "// ApplyV applies a value to values (a thread's start, a primop's callback)."] [270 1 "// ret handles the top frame on a return."] [300 1 "// raiseLam is the code of a thunk whose evaluation raised: entered, it raises again."] [303 1 "// RaiseFree raises its frame's first slot."] [310 1 "// raise raises a synchronous exception (raise#, raiseIO#): the stack unwound to the nearest catch"] [311 1 "// frame, the thunks under evaluation on the way updated to raise it again."] [316 1 "// raiseAsync raises an asynchronous exception in the current thread: the thunks under evaluation on"] [317 1 "// the way reverted to unevaluated (GHC freezes them; the same results)."] [371 1 "// uncaught ends a thread whose exception reached the bottom of its stack (forkIO's and runMainIO's own"] [372 1 "// handlers catch everything, so only a thread started without them gets here: one killed before it ran,"] [373 1 "// which ends silently, as GHC's)."] [380 2 "// a thread killed before it started (forkIO's handler not yet on its stack) ends silently, as GHC's"] [383 1 "// ---- threads ----"] [393 1 "// wake makes a blocked thread runnable."] [403 1 "// block stops the current thread until it is woken; on waking it returns from the blocked call"] [404 1 "// (with the return registers its waker sets) or runs e."] [413 1 "// throwTo raises x in t asynchronously (throwTo#, killThread#)."] [434 1 "// unblock takes a blocked thread out of what it waits on."] [473 1 "// Run runs the program's :Main.main and returns its exit status."] [510 1 "// where describes the current thread's stack for an error message."] [537 1 "// schedule runs threads until until is done (or every thread is)."] [588 1 "// deadlock raises BlockedIndefinitelyOnMVar (or OnSTM) in the threads blocked on MVars (STM) when no"] [589 1 "// thread can run and none waits for time (GHC finds the unreachable ones by its GC; hsi raises in every"] [590 1 "// blocked one, a class)."] [617 1 "// runSlice runs t for a time slice, or until it blocks or ends."] [630 39 "// a transaction is not preempted (HES9 (a))"] [649 1 "// shutdown flushes the standard handles (hs_exit's flushStdHandles) and is the exit status."] [660 1 "// Exit is the program's end requested by shutdownHaskellAndExit: the handles flushed first."] [674 1 "// CFunctions are the C functions hsi's table has."] [683 1 "// PrimopNames are the primops hsi implements."] [692 1 "// Loaded is the number of modules loaded, LoadedBytes their forms' size, Steps the nodes run (by slices)."]] :go/pos {:name [1 9] :package [1 1]} :go/semis [[156 24] [168 27] [212 23] [331 27] [342 27] [360 37] [479 20] [519 27] [519 44]]} (go/file "machine.go" :imports [


